 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? Definitely. Sleep Sounds is the go-to for this. It has soothing sound of waves crashing on the shore, often combined with the gentle hum of night traffic. Then look at the reviews to find one with different narrator. wave sound itself is really soothing. If you struggle to get to sleep or wake up during the night, yes. Set it for about two hours before you want to sleep. Sorry to hear that. Sleep usually comes around firmly, often with practice. If sleeping gets worse, or lasts several nights, pop into your doctor. They' your health team, and they care about you.",
